# Added by cargo
#
# Anchored, and deliberately so. A bare `target` matches a directory of that name
# at ANY depth, which silently swallowed `crates/rts-cranelift/src/target/` — a
# source directory, not a build one. Cargo only ever creates its build directory
# at the workspace root, so anchoring costs nothing and stops the pattern from
# claiming source that happens to share the name.
/target
# `bench/isolated/` is its own cargo root (an empty `[workspace]` table in its
# manifest), so it has a build directory of its own that the anchored `/target`
# above cannot reach. Anchored for the same reason that one is: naming the path
# rather than the directory keeps the pattern from claiming a source directory
# somewhere else that happens to be called `target`.
/bench/isolated/target
debug_*
.claude/settings.local.json

